    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 80548,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80548.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "You know, I think there was a moment there when things really seemed to come apart. And I'm not sure that the Senator from West Virginia was quite ready for the scale of the backlash at that moment. And that's on policy grounds, but it's also just on the grounds that We were all trying to engage in this in good faith for well over a year. And if you're not going to actually make a decision at the end of the day, then that's a very bad place to be. And I think he realized that we were close enough that we could get there and make it work for all 50 senators involved.",
