    "turn_text": "tons of provisions. But one thing, just like this little thing, stuck out to me that if it's passed, it would raise minimum bids for oil and gas leases from $2 to $10 an acre and land rental fees from $150 to $3 an acre and eventually up to $15 an acre. Why does the United States devalue land for extractive industry in this way?",
