    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80548.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "You know, I think there's just an enormous There's an enormous inertia, and this represents actually a step towards actual market-based approaches to these things. As we recognize that they're not going to be around, they can't be around forever, and we have to make this transition. But that doesn't take away from the fact that you have 100 years of economic and cultural inertia. And I see this Almost every economic fight in Washington DC is one between incumbents and innovators, and it's no different in the energy space.",
